meta {
  name: 05 Re-issue activation key
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/centers/me/students/{{studentId}}/activation-key
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 201
}

script:post-response {
  bru.setEnvVar("activationKey", res.body.activationKey);
}

docs {
  For a student who lost their key or whose key expired. The previous key stops
  working the moment this succeeds — verify that by keeping the old value and
  trying it in `Student Activation / 01`.

  The check that matters: run this AFTER the student has activated. It must fail
  with 404 STUDENT_NOT_FOUND_OR_ALREADY_ACTIVE.

  That refusal is load-bearing. Re-keying a live account would let the center
  redeem the new key, set a password, and take the account from its owner. A
  center legitimately holds keys for accounts nobody has claimed yet; this is
  the line that stops it reaching one that has been.
}
